ATS-301 / review item 5 -- the 409 body carries the capability reason
======================================================================

WHAT THIS LOG PROVES
  The review required that a 409 from the capability negotiation carry the
  REASON -- which capability was missing and why -- not just an error code.
  This log shows (a) the HTTP tests assert that, and (b) those assertions are
  NOT tautological: mutating the code that builds the reason turns them red.

THE MUTATION
  server/adapters/registry.mjs -- negotiationFailure() is made to return {},
  so the 409 body keeps only {"error":"<CODE>"} and loses the reason.

--- run 1: the MUTATED tree ---
command: node --test tests/api.test.mjs
exit code: 1

Failing tests under the mutation:
  ✖ IT-API-011: POST /runners with an unsatisfiable capability is 409 WITH the reason (419.2524ms)
  ✖ IT-API-012: POST /runners with a PINNED runner that cannot satisfy the request is 409 WITH the reason (2.5876ms)
  ✖ IT-API-014: POST /run with an unsatisfiable capability is 409 WITH the reason (423.8258ms)

  -> 3 of the 15 API tests go red when the reason is dropped:
     IT-API-011  POST /runners, unpinned
     IT-API-012  POST /runners, pinned runner
     IT-API-014  POST /run
  -> the assertion bodies are not constant: they check the body for
     missing[] / rejected[] and for the adapter's own reason text.

